This directory must exist in the repository, tracked, even when empty.

The modernization-plan agentic workflow is fenced by safe-outputs to
`docs/plans/**` and writes its plan there. The agent sandbox denies every
directory-creation call -- mkdir, install -d, git worktree, the language
runtime equivalents, all of it -- and the `create` tool refuses to create a
file whose parent directory does not exist.

Git does not track empty directories. So without this file, `docs/plans/` is
absent from a fresh checkout on the runner, the agent cannot create it, and the
run fails with `report_incomplete` after burning ~20 minutes. That happened on
run 32746344407 (TIMCNV, 2026-08-24).

Do not delete this file. `tools/preflight.sh` asserts it is tracked.
